/* GENERATED by tools/pack-blobs.py — do not edit by hand.
 *
 * Each mark approximated as 128 circles by greedy medial-axis packing: the
 * deepest point inside the shape is the centre of the largest circle that fits, so take
 * it, erase that disc, repeat. Unioned as a metaball field they read as the letter;
 * pulled together they read as one mass.
 *
 * Both marks carry the same count, so blob i simply has a home in each shape and
 * travels between them. That is what makes the transition seamless by construction:
 * there is never a second shape to cross-fade with, only one surface following the
 * blobs that define it.
 *
 * Coordinates are in the shared frame's own space — x spans ±aspect/2, y spans ±0.5,
 * radius is a fraction of frame height. Sorted left to right so the swarm drifts
 * coherently rather than shuffling.
 */

